{
  "summary": "User Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst) reports Excel shows \"Unlicensed Product\" and editing is restricted. Checked: account active, not locked, no failed logins, password set 2026-09-11, no must-change flag. Sign-in logs for last 14 days show only successful m365 sign-ins (corporate network, Duo push MFA), so the account is signing in correctly. Laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) is online, 14.6% disk free, no warnings. Mailbox is 99.4% full (50.9 GB of 51.2 GB), noted but not a licensing cause. Per KB-026 escalate condition (signs in correctly but still sees Unlicensed product, license may not be assigned), needs Tier 2 to verify the Microsoft 365 license assignment for mei.chen@brightline.example and check Office activation on BL-LT-0109. Not yet done on the user side: sign out of all Office apps, reopen, sign in with company email; results not confirmed.",
  "reason": "KB-026 escalation condition met: user signs in correctly but Office still reports Unlicensed product, so the license assignment needs checking by Tier 2."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for reporting this. I checked your account and your sign-ins to Microsoft 365 are succeeding, so the account itself is fine. The 'Unlicensed Product' message usually means the Office license needs to be checked on the Microsoft side, so I've passed your ticket to our second-tier team to verify it. While you wait, please try this: in any Office app, go to File, Account, sign out, close all Office apps, reopen, and sign in with your company email. Also, your mailbox is nearly full (about 99%), so you may want to clear out some old mail or attachments. Let us know if the message is still there after signing in again.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user (active, not locked, 0 failed logins, no must-change flag, password set 2026-09-11), 14-day sign-in logs (all successful m365 and VPN sign-ins with Duo push, corporate and residential networks, no anomalies), and device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15, online, 14.6% disk free, no warnings). Per KB-026 the user signs in correctly but still sees Unlicensed product, so escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) to verify the M365 license assignment and Office activation. User has not yet confirmed they tried the sign-out/reopen step. Side note: mailbox at 99.4% of quota (50.9 of 51.2 GB), which may cause other Outlook issues. Not a licensing cause.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-026"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
